{title: 485 - I Must Tell Jesus}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #485 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 485}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F#m]I must tell Jesus [A7/G]all of [F#m]my trials;
[F#m]I can [A7/G]not bear [D/F#]these burdens [A7/G]alone,
[F#m]In my distress [A]He kindly [D/F#]will [A7/G]help me,
[F#m]He ever loves [A7/G]and [D/F#]cares [Dm/F]for His [F#m]own.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F#m]I must tell Jesus! [D/F#]I must tell Jesus!
[D]I cannot bear [G/D]my burdens alone;
[D/A]I [A7]must tell Jesus! I must [F#m]tell Jesus!
[A7/G]Jesus can [D/F#]help me, Jesus [Dm/F]alone.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F#m]I must tell Jesus [D/F#]all [A7/G]of my [F#m]troubles,
[F#m]He is [A7/G]a kind, [D/F#]compassionate [F#m]Friend;
[F#m]If I but ask [A]Him He will [D/F#]deliver,
[F#m]Make of my [A7/G]troubles [D/F#]quickly [Dm/F]an [F#m]end.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F#m]Oh, how the world to [D/F#]evil [A7/G]allures [F#m]me!
[F#m]Oh, how [A7/G]my heart [D/F#]is tempted [A7/G]to [F#m]sin!
[F#m]I must tell Jesus, [A]and He [D/F#]will [A7/G]help me
[F#m]Over the [A7/G]world the [D/F#]vict'ry [Dm/F]to [F#m]win.
{end_of_verse}
